# Walk-then-interact (hard law)

Every **world-space** tap that opens dialogue, shop, board, info, quest flag, or map travel MUST walk the player into range first. Far taps never fire the act instantly.

## Required choke points

Use `StoryWorldHooks` only — do not invent a parallel walk:

| Target | API |
|--------|-----|
| NPC | `story.approachNpcThen(node, act)` |
| Building / sign / prop / portal | `story.approachInteractThen(node, act)` |

`findInteract` / `findNpc` helpers MUST return the hit `node` so the caller can pass it into these APIs.

## Pattern

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const hit = SomeWorldLayout.findInteract(world, wx, wy);
if (hit) {
  story.approachInteractThen(hit.node, () => {
    if (!hit.node.isValid) return;
    // openShop / tryBuilding / travelTo / openInfo / noteFlag …
  });
  return;
}

// ❌ BAD — instant fire from across the map
if (hit) {
  storyDlg.tryBuilding(hit.key);
  shopPanel.openShop(hit.shopId);
  travelTo('mine', …);
  return;
}
```

## Exceptions (do NOT wrap)

- UI / HUD / modal taps (`handleTap` on panels, quest dock claim, dialogue advance)
- Free-roam empty-ground taps — stick only (`TouchJoystick`); no click-to-move
- Quest idle world aims — `TutorialGuide.questClickMoveDest` + `ClickMoveMarker.go` walk to the guide feet goal (starlight path / place ring)
- Farm gather/chop/dig already walks via `FarmSystem` + `PlayerController.walkTo` — keep that path; do not double-wrap
- `ClickMoveMarker` / `walkTo` also for approachInteract / approachNpc

Indoor leave (`door_exit` / `exit_floor_glow`) is tap-driven like outdoor enter — never collision/`EXIT_ZONE` auto-travel.

## When adding a new map / POI / quest building

1. Hit-test returns `{ …, node }`.
2. `GameBootstrap` (or the map’s tap handler) calls `approachNpcThen` / `approachInteractThen`.
3. Put side effects **only** inside the arrive callback.
4. Stand feet for new building names go in `StoryWorldHooks.standForInteract` (and TutorialGuide aims stay in sync).

If a tap opens content without going through these helpers, it is a bug — fix the choke point, do not special-case one quest.
